	(text "Elevation Axis"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 165.1 34.544 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6bb970be-2ec5-442b-aca3-c30ea5869565")
	)
	(text "ELEVATION SENSING: Firgelli Hall quadrature into RoboClaw EN1 (motor M1)\n\nWiring, J8 to A1 (RoboClaw):\n  J8-1  RC_5V        Hall sensor supply from the RoboClaw 5VDC output (800 mA max, shared).\n                     D21 SMF6.0A clamps it.\n  J8-2  EL_ENC_A_IN  Hall A. R47 5.1k pull-up to RC_5V, D16 ESD clamp, R49 100R + C57 10nF \n                     -> EN1_A (A1 1A).\n  J8-3  EL_ENC_B_IN  Hall B. R51 5.1k pull-up to RC_5V, D18 ESD clamp, R53 100R + C59 10nF \n                     -> EN1_B (A1 1B).\n  J8-4  PGND         Sensor return, on the RoboClaw ground.\nThe pull-ups suit open-collector Hall outputs and are harmless with push-pull outputs.\nThe 100R/10nF filters (tau = 1 us, about 160 kHz) pass the Hall pulses and remove cable noise and ringing.\nRoboClaw inputs tolerate 5 V, so no level shifting is needed.\n\nHow the RoboClaw uses it:\n  - The two Hall sensors are 90 degrees apart (quadrature A/B). The RoboClaw counts the pulses, and\n    the A/B phase gives the direction. If the count falls while the actuator extends, swap A/B in\n    Motion Studio; no rewiring is needed.\n  - Position = encoder count. Speed = count rate. Set QPPS (counts/s at full speed) in Motion\n    Studio, then auto-tune the M1 velocity and position PID.\n  - The encoder is incremental, so the count is lost at power-off and the axis must be homed at\n    start-up. The actuator has no limit switches. Home on the elevation limit switch (J12 -> S4, set as\n    home/limit), or drive slowly to full retraction with a low current limit, then zero the counter.\n  - Stroke = counts / (Firgelli pulses per inch). Elevation angle follows from the mount geometry,\n    which is non-linear, so convert between angle and counts on the CM4."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 158.496 106.934 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7da812a7-2688-406d-aba8-de845f48a90a")
	)
	(text "AZIMUTH SENSING: AS5600 analog absolute angle into RoboClaw EN2 (motor M2)\n\nWiring, J9 to A1 (RoboClaw):\n  J9-1  AZ_ENC_3V3  AS5600 supply: U18 3.3 V LDO (from RC_5V) via F3 (100 mA PTC), D23 clamp.\n                    Run the AS5600 at 3.3 V (VDD5V tied to VDD3V3 on the sensor board).\n  J9-2  AZ_ENC_IN   AS5600 OUT. D22 ESD clamp. R57 68k / R58 100k divider (x0.595) -> EN2_A (A1 2A).\n                    C62 100nF filters it (40.5k x 100nF, tau = 4 ms, about 39 Hz).\n  J9-3  PGND        Sensor return.\n  EN2_B is unused; the analog signal needs one channel only.\nScaling: AS5600 0-3.3 V -> 0-1.96 V at EN2_A, inside the RoboClaw 0-2 V analog input range.\n\nHow the RoboClaw uses it:\n  - Set EN2 to Absolute encoder mode in Motion Studio. The voltage is an absolute angle, so no\n    homing is needed at power-up.\n  - M2 runs position PID on this reading. Speed is derived from the rate of change of position;\n    there is no separate speed sensor.\n  - Read the RoboClaw position value at each end of travel and set those as the M2 min/max position limits.\n  - The AS5600 is single-turn: its output jumps at the 0/360 deg wrap. Fit the magnet so the azimuth\n    travel never crosses the wrap, or set ZPOS/MPOS (I2C or OTP) to place the range. A crossing\n    makes the position loop run away.\n  - The magnet must be on a shaft that turns at most one revolution over the full azimuth travel.\n\nAS5600 output loading (datasheet): full-range analog (the default) needs >= 100k. R57 + R58 = 168k, OK.\n  - OUT capacitive load 1 nF max: R57 isolates C62; keep the J9 cable short (about 100 pF/m).\n  - Divider source impedance is about 40k. If the RoboClaw EN2 pull-up stays on in Absolute mode it lifts\n    the reading: bench-check EN2_A with and without the RoboClaw; calibrate travel limits on hardware.\n  - J9 is powered from 3V3_CM4 (logic GND) but returns on PGND, so the sensor current crosses NT1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 24.638 101.6 0)
		(effects
